      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Latitudes are imaginary parallel circles running East to West, measuring distance North or South from the Equator (0°).",
        "Longitudes are semi-circles running North to South meeting at the poles, used primarily to calculate time.",
        "The Earth rotates 360° in 24 hours, which corresponds to 15° per hour or 1° every 4 minutes.",
        "Indian Standard Time (IST) is derived from 82.5° E longitude passing through Mirzapur, Uttar Pradesh.",
        "Crossing the International Date Line (180° Meridian) results in a change of one full calendar day."
